"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nThe weather was so hot that all I could think about was refreshing makguksu (buckwheat noodles).  \nSo once again, we set out to find a makguksu restaurant.  \n\nLooking it up, it was quite a famous place known for having inevitable waiting lines, so we headed there with some apprehension.  \n\nIt turned out there was no separate reservation system, and phone reservations were not accepted if there was a wait.  \nThere was ample parking space in front of the restaurant, but if the crowd got larger, double parking seemed likely necessary.  \n\nFortunately, the timing was great, so we were seated immediately without waiting.  \nShortly after we arrived and placed our order, the entire restaurant filled up in an instant.  \n\nWe ordered Bibim Makguksu, Perilla Seed Makguksu (Large Portion), and Vegetable Buckwheat Pancake.  \n\nAfter waiting just a little while, the vegetable buckwheat pancake was served quickly first.  \nI had eaten vegetable pancakes many times, but this was my first time having one made with buckwheat flour.  \nAs expected, it was crispy and delicious, with a deep aroma of buckwheat.  \n\nSeeing us enjoy the buckwheat pancake, the neighboring table ordered one additionally as well.  \n\nRight around when we finished most of the pancake, the makguksu dishes were served.  \n\nThe Bibim Makguksu was milder and less spicy or overwhelming than expected.  \nIt was served with gentle dongchimi (radish water kimchi) broth, which was also pleasantly light and refreshing.  \nYou can add seasonings to your preference, but we only added a tiny bit.  \n\nThe Perilla Seed Makguksu had plenty of perilla oil, which I really enjoyed.  \nIt had lots of perilla seeds as well, making it exceptionally savory and nutty.  \nIt was exactly the classic perilla seed makguksu flavor you would expect.  \n\nCompared to Namgyeong Makguksu, it was less sweet and on the subtler, milder side.  \nPersonally, the style of Namgyeong Makguksu suited my taste a bit more.  \n\nStill, it was definitely a place worthy of being called a great restaurant.  \n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"